{
  "0": "Feature construction: scale each nonpadding input item embedding by 1 + 0.1*tanh(z_i), where z_i is standardized log1p item frequency computed solely from that category's training interactions. Keep padding zero and candidate embeddings unchanged. This bounded frequency feature may help SASRec distinguish common from niche history items without a separate scorer. Preserve learned embeddings, topology, readout, loss and optimizer; save training frequency statistics for identical prediction.",
  "1": "Network architecture: replace each SASRec feed-forward sublayer with a hidden_dim → 4*hidden_dim → hidden_dim MLP using GELU, retaining existing dropout, residual connections and normalization placement. Greater nonlinear capacity may capture diverse purchase patterns, especially in Electronics. Preserve causal attention, block count, input features, embeddings, scoring, readout, loss and optimizer; update the predictor writer to reconstruct this single-model architecture.",
  "2": "Sequence modeling: double the baseline maximum history length for all four categories, retaining the most recent interactions in chronological order and the existing causal mask, padding convention and position representation. Longer context may recover recurring preferences missing from short histories. Change only context length and the required positional-table/checkpoint shapes; preserve embedding width, Transformer topology, readout, loss and optimizer, with identical truncation at prediction.",
  "3": "Training strategy: retain the baseline optimizer and peak learning rate, but apply linear learning-rate warmup over epochs 1–5 followed by cosine decay to 10% of the peak at epoch 200. Smoother early updates and smaller late updates may reduce validation fluctuations and Electronics overfitting. Preserve seed 42, epoch cap 200, batch size, dropout, weight decay, architecture, features, loss and validation-based selection of one checkpoint per category."
}
